### Step 7 — Ratings, comments, saved recipes, subscriptions. VS Code "REST Client".
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Log in as a demo cook
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "identifier": "chef_kabir", "password": "Cookify2026!" }

### 2. Rate recipe 1 (re-rating replaces your score; you can't rate your own)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/1/rating
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "score": 5 }

### 3. Remove your rating
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/1/rating
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4. Comment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/1/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "Crispy perfection — added extra ghee!" }

### 5. Comments (public, newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/1/comments

### 6. Save / unsave
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/1/save
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7. My saved recipes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/saved
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8. Subscribe to a cook → { following, followerCount }
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/chef_meera/follow
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 9. Profile with follower counts and "following" flag
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/chef_meera
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 10. Unsubscribe
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/chef_meera/follow
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
